    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n******UNDER OFFER*****\nNestled in a peaceful hillside setting with outstanding views of the surrounding countryside, this delightful two-bedroom detached cottage sits on a generous c. 0.88 acre site, offering privacy, space, and superb potential for future extension. Ideally located just 3km from the village of Knocknagoshel and 9km from Castleisland, the property combines rural tranquility with convenient access to nearby amenities.\nThe accommodation comprises an entrance hallway, a lounge/sitting room, a kitchen/dining area, utility room, two double bedrooms, and bathroom with w/c and whb. The living areas benefit from a desirable south-facing aspect, ensuring excellent natural light throughout the day.\nTo the front, a covered decking area provides an ideal space for outdoor dining and relaxation, perfect for entertaining or enjoying the surrounding countryside views.\nExternally, the expansive site offers excellent scope for further development or extension, making this an attractive option for those seeking to create a long-term family home. A detached double garage to the rear adds exceptional value, providing ample space for storage, a workshop, DIY projects, or hobby use.\nAdditional features include oil-fired central heating, uPVC throughout, and connection to all essential services.\nViewing is highly recommended and is strictly by appointment only."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hallway - 6.00m x 1.01m\nwith glazed door and oak style linoleum flooring\n\nLounge / Sitting Room - 4.06m x 3.01m\nwith fitted insert stove, carpet flooring and window\n\nKitchen / Dining Room - 4.35m x 3.05m\nContemporary kitchen with matt grey units, quartzite-style work surface, oak-effect linoleum flooring, wall tiling and range. 2 windows. Access to 5m x 5m covered deck area\n\nUtility Room - 2.19m x 1.39m\nWith fitted units, washing machine, sink, floor and wall tiles and window.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.32m x 3.02m\nDouble bedroom with carpet flooring and window\n\nBedroom 2 - 2.84m x 2.22m\nDouble bedroom with carpet flooring and window\n\nBathroom - 2.21m x 1.51m\nWith Triton Novel electric shower, wall tiles, porcelain wall tiles, w/c, whb and window\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>A peaceful and tranquil setting that enjoys wonderful views of the surrounding countrywide </li><li>2-bedroom detached cottage on a c. 0.88 acre site in a peaceful countryside setting</li><li>South-facing living areas</li><li>Covered decking area to the front </li><li>Detached double garage providing excellent storage, workshop, or hobby space</li><li>Convenient location 3km from Knocknagoshel and 9km from Castleisland</li><li>Oil heating, uPVC windows, and all services connected</li><li>The BER assessor advises that changing the existing boiler unit to a condensing boiler and installing a room and water thermostat will bring the energy rating up to a ' C'</ul>"
      },
